  54: ## T3 — Fail-closed create and fence budgets with winning-insert quota
  55: Reasoning: D1 makes replays quota-free, which needs separate, non-bypassable budgets; the current limiter is 
fail-open and counts attempts, not insertions.
  56: Task: The insertion quota is charged in the same transaction as a winning insertion (once among concurrent 
same-key requests; never more stored messages than the quota with distinct keys at the boundary; not charged for 
replays); every authenticated create request — including malformed bodies, early-validation failures, replays, and 
quota losers — consumes a per-user request budget whose charge survives an insertion rollback; fence/lookup calls 
consume their own per-user budget; any exhausted budget returns 429; a budget that cannot be checked refuses the 
request as 429 (D4 planning decision).
  57: Done when: The AC-009 route-level clauses hold on the local database, including under a real limiter 
permission/availability failure.
  58: Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests for each AC-009 route clause plus malformed-body and early-validation 
charging, rollback survival, and a limiter failure (revoked/unavailable function) producing 429; Phase 4/legacy 
